eport.md so the grader can interpret.\n\nLet me write everything now.\n\nLet me also double-check the reverse complement computation once more with the script (trust but verify output).\n\nAlso for p02 forward \"GCTGACCTGACTGACCTGAA\" — verify length 20: G-C-T-G-A-C-C-T-G-A-C-T-G-A-C-C-T-G-A-A = 20 ✓. p02 reverse \"CTATTCAGGTCAGTCAGGTC\" = 20 ✓. p01 reverse \"TCATTCAGGTCAGTCAGGTC\" 20 ✓.\n\nInteresting: p01 vs p02 reverse differ only at position 2 (T vs C): TCATTC... vs CTATTC... wait: p01 R = T C A T T C A G G T C A G T C A G G T C; p02 R = C T A T T C A G G T C A G T C A G G T C. So p02 R is p01 R with the first two characters swapped (TC→CT). Their RC differs at the last two positions: p01 RC ends ...GAATGA; p02 RC ends ...GAATAG. Exactly the canonical vs alt tail difference (GAATGA vs GAATAG). Nice, consistent with isoform-specific design.\n\nAnd p01 F = first 20 nt; p02 F = positions 4-23. Both pair with the tail RC to give: p01: 1→102 = 102 bp; p02: 4→102 = 99 bp. Expected 108/104. Differences: -6, -5.\n\nHmm, interesting: if the transcripts were 6 nt longer (e.g. tail GAATGA + extra), expected would match... e.g. if canonical were 108 long, p01 amplicon 1-108 = 108 ✓. And if alt were... p02 expects 104: 4→107 → alt length would need to be 107? 102+5. Hmm, not uniform. Whatever — the supplied sequences are the ground truth; we report the discrepancies.\n\nActually wait — maybe the intended reading is: the FASTA sequences are truncated relative to metadata (CDS=101-700 suggests full transcript ≥700). So expected_product_bp was computed on the full-length transcript, but the supplied FASTA is a truncated excerpt — that's the \"internally inconsistent metadata\" scenario: we must NOT repair by assuming a longer sequence; we report the inconsistency. Our audit on the supplied sequences gives 102/99 with flags. This aligns with the task's warning. Good.\n\nOK let me write the files now. First check python.\n\nAfter running, verify:\n- output/primer_audit.csv exists with exact header and 3 rows.\n- output/report.md exists.\n- output/analysis.py exists (obviously).\n\nThen final answer: summary of findings.\n\nLet me write analysis.py now. I'll be careful with the here-string. Python uses double quotes heavily; single-quoted PS here-string @'...'@ passes everything literally. \n\nOne concern: does the code contain the sequence `'@`? No line starts with `'@`. Fine.\n\nLet me fully draft the final Python code:\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Audit primer pairs against the supplied transcript isoforms.\n\nInputs (the only data used by this audit):\n    inputs/primer_candidates.csv\n        columns: pair_id, forward, reverse, expected_transcript, expected_product_bp\n    inputs/transcripts.fa\n        FASTA; headers carry metadata such as CDS=<start>-<end>.\n\nOutputs:\n    output/primer_audit.csv\n        columns: pair_id, transcripts_matched, amplicon_length, cds_compatible, status, reason\n    output/report.md\n        human-readable audit report.\n\nRules implemented here:\n    * Only the supplied sequences are used; nothing is fetched or inferred from\n      external databases.\n    * Primer matching is exact (no mismatches, no gaps). The reverse primer is\n      matched as its reverse complement against the sense strand.\n    * Malformed or internally inconsistent sequence metadata (for example a CDS\n      range that extends past the end of the sequence) is *reported*, never\n      silently repaired or clamped.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport csv\nimport re\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nWORKSPACE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nINPUT_DIR = WORKSPACE / \"inputs\"\nOUTPUT_DIR = WORKSPACE / \"output\"\n\nPRIMER_CSV = INPUT_DIR / \"primer_candidates.csv\"\nFASTA_PATH = INPUT_DIR / \"transcripts.fa\"\nAUDIT_CSV = OUTPUT_DIR / \"primer_audit.csv\"\nREPORT_MD = OUTPUT_DIR / \"report.md\"\n\nCOMPLEMENT = str.maketrans(\"ACGT\", \"TGCA\")\nCDS_RE = re.compile(r\"CDS=(\\d+)-(\\d+)\")\n\n\ndef revcomp(seq: str) -> str:\n    return seq.translate(COMPLEMENT)[::-1]\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# FASTA parsing / metadata validation\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef parse_fasta(path: Path) -> list[dict]:\n    records: list[dict] = []\n    current: dict | None = None\n    chunks: list[str] = []\n\n    def close():\n        nonlocal current, chunks\n        if current is not None:\n            current[\"seq\"] = \"\".join(chunks).upper()\n            records.append(current)\n        current = None\n        chunks = []\n\n    with path.open(encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n        for lineno, raw in enumerate(fh, 1):\n            line = raw.strip()\n            if not line:\n                continue\n            if line.startswith(\">\"):\n                close()\n                header = line[1:].strip()\n                ident = header.split()[0] if header else f\"NOID_LINE{lineno}\"\n                current = {\n                    \"id\": ident,\n                    \"header\": header,\n                    \"seq\": \"\",\n                    \"cds\": None,\n                    \"seq_issues\": [],\n                    \"cds_issues\": [],\n                }\n                m = CDS_RE.search(header)\n                if m:\n                    current[\"cds\"] = (int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2)))\n            else:\n                if current is None:\n                    raise ValueError(f\"{path.name} line {lineno}: sequence before header\")\n                seq = line.upper()\n                bad = sorted(set(seq) - set(\"ACGT\"))\n                if bad:\n                    current[\"seq_issues\"].append(\n                        f\"invalid characters {bad} at line {lineno}\")\n                chunks.append(seq)\n    close()\n    return records\n\n\ndef validate_record(rec: dict) -> dict:\n    n = len(rec[\"seq\"])\n    if n == 0:\n        rec[\"seq_issues\"].append(\"sequence is empty\")\n    cds = rec[\"cds\"]\n    if cds is None:\n        rec[\"cds_issues\"].append(\"no CDS=<start>-<end> annotation present in header\")\n    else:\n        s, e = cds\n        if s < 1:\n            rec[\"cds_issues\"].append(f\"CDS start {s} is < 1\")\n        if s > e:\n            rec[\"cds_issues\"].append(f\"CDS start {s} > CDS end {e}\")\n        elif e > n:\n            rec[\"cds_issues\"].append(\n                f\"annotated CDS={s}-{e} extends past the end of the {n} bp sequence \"\n                f\"(CDS span {e - s + 1} bp cannot fit inside a {n} bp transcript)\")\n        elif (e - s + 1) % 3 != 0:\n            rec[\"cds_issues\"].append(\n                f\"CDS span {e - s + 1} bp is not a multiple of 3\")\n    rec[\"consistent\"] = not rec[\"seq_issues\"] and not rec[\"cds_issues\"]\n    return rec\n```\n\nHmm wait: treating \"no CDS annotation\" as a cds_issue might be aggressive, but in this task both records have CDS; if missing it's indeed a metadata gap worth reporting. But \"consistent\" would be False in that case — acceptable semantics (\"metadata incomplete\"). Fine.\n\n```python\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Primer matching\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\ndef find_all(haystack: str, needle: str) -> list[int]:\n    hits = []\n    i = haystack.find(needle)\n    while i != -1:\n        hits.append(i + 1)  # 1-based coordinate\n        i = haystack.find(needle, i + 1)\n    return hits\n\n\ndef audit_pair(pair: dict, records: list[dict]) -> dict:\n    fwd = pair[\"forward\"]\n    rev_rc = revcomp(pair[\"reverse\"])\n    audit = {\"fwd_hits\": {}, \"rev_hits\": {}, \"amplicons\": {}}\n    for rec in records:\n        f_hits = find_all(rec[\"seq\"], fwd)\n        r_hits = find_all(rec[\"seq\"], rev_rc)\n        audit[\"fwd_hits\"][rec[\"id\"]] = f_hits\n        audit[\"rev_hits\"][rec[\"id\"]] = r_hits\n        amps = []\n        for f in f_hits:\n            for r in r_hits:\n                r_end = r + len(pair[\"reverse\"]) - 1\n                if r > f:\n                    amps.append({\"start\": f, \"end\": r_end, \"length\": r_end - f + 1})\n        if amps:\n            audit[\"amplicons\"][rec[\"id\"]] = amps\n    return audit\n```\n\nThen evaluation:\n\n```python\nSTATUS_ORDER = [\"pass\", \"length_mismatch\", \"no_binding\", \"off_target\", \"ambiguous\",\n                \"cds_incompatible\", \"metadata_conflict\", \"expected_transcript_missing\",\n                \"malformed_input\"]\n\n\ndef evaluate_pair(pair: dict, audit: dict, records: list[dict]) -> dict:\n    rec_by_id = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in records}\n    expected = pair[\"expected_transcript\"]\n    expected_bp = pair[\"expected_product_bp\"]\n    matched = list(audit[\"amplicons\"].keys())\n    exp_rec = rec_by_id.get(expected)\n    exp_amps = audit[\"amplicons\"].get(expected, []) if exp_rec else []\n\n    reasons: list[str] = []\n    notes: list[str] = []\n\n    # primer binding notes (all supplied transcripts)\n    fwd_txs = [t for t in audit[\"fwd_hits\"] if audit[\"fwd_hits\"][t]]\n    rev_txs = [t for t in audit[\"rev_hits\"] if audit[\"rev_hits\"][t]]\n\n    amp_len = \"\"\n    cds_verdict = \"na\"\n\n    if pair.get(\"input_issue\"):\n        status = \"malformed_input\"\n        reasons.append(pair[\"input_issue\"])\n    elif exp_rec is None:\n        status = \"expected_transcript_missing\"\n        reasons.append(f\"expected transcript '{expected}' is not among the supplied sequences\")\n    elif not matched:\n        status = \"no_binding\"\n        ...\n```\n\nHmm wait, p03's exp_rec exists (TX_CANONICAL). matched = [] → no_binding. Reason details: forward hits none anywhere; RC(reverse) hits none anywhere.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n```python\n    elif not matched:\n        status = \"no_binding\"\n        n_tx = len(records)\n        fwd_any = any(audit[\"fwd_hits\"].values())\n        rev_any = any(audit[\"rev_hits\"].values())\n        detail = []\n        if not fwd_any:\n            detail.append(\"forward primer has no exact match in any supplied transcript\")\n        if not rev_any:\n            detail.append(\"reverse-complement of reverse primer has no exact match in any supplied transcript\")\n        if fwd_any and not rev_any ... etc.\n        reasons.append(\"; \".join(detail) + \"; no amplicon can be formed\")\n```\n\nFor p03: both have no match → \"forward primer has no exact match in any supplied transcript; reverse-complement of reverse primer has no exact match in any supplied transcript; no amplicon can be formed.\"\n\n```python\n    elif not exp_amps:\n        status = \"off_target\"\n        amp_len = audit[\"amplicons\"][matched[0]][0][\"length\"]\n        reasons.append(\n            f\"primers amplify only non-expected transcript(s) {matched}, \"\n            f\"not {expected}\")\n    else:\n        # amplicon on expected transcript exists\n        n_amps = len(exp_amps)\n        if n_amps > 1 or len(audit[\"fwd_hits\"][expected]) > 1 or len(audit[\"rev_hits\"][expected]) > 1:\n            status = \"ambiguous\"\n            amp_len = exp_amps[0][\"length\"]\n            reasons.append(f\"{n_amps} candidate amplicons on {expected}; binding sites not unique\")\n        else:\n            amp = exp_amps[0]\n            amp_len = amp[\"length\"]\n            if amp[\"length\"] != expected_bp:\n                status = \"length_mismatch\"\n                reasons.append(\n                    f\"amplicon on {expected} is {amp['length']} bp \"\n                    f\"(coordinates {amp['start']}..{amp['end']}), expected {expected_bp} bp \"\n                    f\"(difference {amp['length'] - expected_bp:+d} bp)\")\n            else:\n                # length ok; check CDS\n                cds_v = cds compatibility...\n                if cds issues: status = \"metadata_conflict\"\n                elif within cds: status = \"pass\"\n                else: status = \"cds_incompatible\"\n```\n\nBinding position notes for reason: add to notes list:\n\n```python\n    if exp_rec is not None:\n        fh_ = audit[\"fwd_hits\"].get(expected, [])\n        rh_ = audit[\"rev_hits\"].get(expected, [])\n        L = len(pair[\"forward\"])\n        if fh_:\n            notes.append(f\"forward primer binds {expected} at \" + \",\".join(f\"{p}..{p+L-1}\" for p in fh_))\n        else:\n            notes.append(f\"forward primer does not bind {expected}\")\n        ...\n```\n\nHmm, let me keep reasons focused. Let me assemble the reason as: binding summary; amplicon summary; metadata summary; specificity summary. Compose a list of sentences.\n\nLet me simplify and write concrete reason builders:\n\nFor each pair, build:\n1. Binding sentence: for the expected transcript: \"forward binds TX_CANONICAL uniquely at 1..20; reverse primer (as reverse complement) binds TX_CANONICAL uniquely at 83..102.\" If not applicable: \"forward/reverse has no exact match in TX_CANONICAL (or any transcript).\"\n2. Amplicon sentence: \"Predicted amplicon TX_CANONICAL:1..102 = 102 bp vs expected 108 bp (delta -6 bp) → length mismatch.\" or \"no amplicon.\"\n3. Specificity: \"No amplicon predicted on TX_ALT.\" (list the other transcripts) — only if there are other transcripts.\n4. Metadata: \"Header metadata of TX_CANONICAL is internally inconsistent: CDS=101-700 exceeds sequence length 102 bp; reported as-is, not repaired → cds_compatible=inconsistent_metadata.\"\n\nThat's thorough. Let me code it generically.\n\ncds_compatible determination:\n\n```python\ndef cds_compatible_verdict(rec, amps):\n    \"\"\"Return (value, explanation).\"\"\"\n    if not amps:\n        return \"na\", \"no amplicon, nothing to evaluate against the CDS\"\n    if rec[\"cds\"] is None:\n        return \"na\", \"transcript header carries no CDS annotation\"\n    if rec[\"cds_issues\"]:\n        return \"inconsistent_metadata\", (\n            f\"CDS annotation CDS={rec['cds'][0]}-{rec['cds'][1]} is internally inconsistent \"\n            f\"with the {len(rec['seq'])} bp sequence; compatibility cannot be assessed\")\n    s, e = rec[\"cds\"]\n    if all(a[\"start\"] >= s and a[\"end\"] <= e for a in amps):\n        return \"yes\", f\"amplicon lies within annotated CDS {s}..{e}\"\n    return \"no\", f\"amplicon extends outside annotated CDS {s}..{e}\"\n```\n\nFor p01: rec has cds_issues → \"inconsistent_metadata\". Also let me add a note in the reason about the face-value containment: even taking CDS=101-700 at face value, amplicon 1..102 is not contained in 101..700. I can compute the face-value containment and add to explanation: \"even taking the annotation at face value, amplicon 1..102 is not contained within CDS 101..700.\" Nice touch — shows we didn't silently repair. Add it when cds_issues exist and face-value containment fails.\n\nNow the main():\n\n```python\ndef load_primers(path):\n    pairs = []\n    with path.open(newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n        reader = csv.DictReader(fh)\n        required = [\"pair_id\", \"forward\", \"reverse\", \"expected_transcript\", \"expected_product_bp\"]\n        missing = [c for c in required if c not in (reader.fieldnames or [])]\n        if missing:\n            raise ValueError(f\"primer CSV missing columns: {missing}\")\n        for rownum, row in enumerate(reader, 2):\n            pair = {k: (v or \"\").strip() for k, v in row.items() if k}\n            issues = []\n            pair[\"forward\"] = pair[\"forward\"].upper()\n            pair[\"reverse\"] = pair[\"reverse\"].upper()\n            if not re.fullmatch(r\"[ACGT]+\", pair[\"forward\"]):\n                issues.append(\"forward primer is not valid DNA (ACGT)\")\n            if not re.fullmatch(r\"[ACGT]+\", pair[\"reverse\"]):\n                issues.append(\"reverse primer is not valid DNA (ACGT)\")\n            try:\n                pair[\"expected_product_bp\"] = int(pair[\"expected_product_bp\"])\n            except ValueError:\n                issues.append(\"expected_product_bp is not an integer\")\n                pair[\"expected_product_bp\"] = None\n            pair[\"input_issue\"] = \"; \".join(issues) if issues else None\n            pairs.append(pair)\n    return pairs\n```\n\nMain flow:\n\n```python\ndef main():\n    OUTPUT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    records = [validate_record(r) for r in parse_fasta(FASTA_PATH)]\n    pairs = load_primers(PRIMER_CSV)\n\n    rows = []\n    details = []\n    for pair in pairs:\n        audit = audit_pair(pair, records) if not pair[\"input_issue\"] else empty audit\n        ev = evaluate_pair(pair, audit, records)\n        rows.append(ev[\"csv_row\"])\n        details.append(ev)\n\n    write csv\n    write report\n    print console summary\n```\n\nReport generation: build Markdown with sections. Include:\n\n- Title, generation timestamp? Avoid non-determinism? Either way; I'll include date from datetime.\n- Inputs table.\n- Metadata integrity section: for each record: header, length, CDS annotation, issues (bullet). Emphasize: \"reported, not repaired\".\n- Methods bullet.\n- Per-pair detail: binding positions, amplicon, expected vs observed, cds verdict, status.\n- Summary table (same content as CSV).\n- Status vocabulary legend.\n\nOK let me write it all out concretely. I'll now write the code in one go and test.\n\nOne more detail: `evaluate_pair` also needs the pair's primer sequences for position calculation (length of forward for the binding site range). Fine.\n\nAlso for the no_binding reason for p03, mention the homopolymer nature? Generic code won't phrase it that way; the generic sentence is sufficient.\n\nLet me also compute for the report the primer binding on non-expected transcripts (e.g. p01 forward binds TX_ALT at 1..20 but no product). Let me include a \"primer-level binding\" subsection per pair: list per transcript the fwd hits and rev hits.\n\nTime to write. I'll write the file with a PowerShell here-string via WriteAllText (no BOM, UTF8 without BOM):\n\n$script = @'\n...python...\n'@\nNew-Item -ItemType Directory -Force output | Out-Null\n[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText(\"$PWD\\output\\analysis.py\", $script, (New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding($false)))\n\nThen run: python output\\analysis.py\n\nThen Get-Content output\\primer_audit.csv and report.md.\n\nLet me finalize the Python code text.\n\nAlso careful with Python version: the `list[dict]` type hint needs 3.9+. With `from __future__ import annotations`, annotations become strings so it's fine on 3.7+. OK.\n\nLet me draft evaluate_pair fully:\n\n```python\ndef evaluate_pair(pair, audit, records):\n    rec_by_id = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in records}\n    expected = pair[\"expected_transcript\"]\n    expected_bp = pair[\"expected_product_bp\"]\n    matched = list(audit[\"amplicons\"].keys())\n    exp_rec = rec_by_id.get(expected)\n    exp_amps = audit[\"amplicons\"].get(expected, []) if exp_rec else []\n\n    sentences = []\n\n    # ---- primer binding summary on expected transcript\n    if exp_rec is not None:\n        L_f = len(pair[\"forward\"])\n        L_r = len(pair[\"reverse\"])\n        fhits = audit[\"fwd_hits\"].get(expected, [])\n        rhits = audit[\"rev_hits\"].get(expected, [])\n        if fhits:\n            coord = \", \".join(f\"{p}-{p + L_f - 1}\" for p in fhits)\n            uniq = \"uniquely \" if len(fhits) == 1 else \"\"\n            sentences.append(f\"forward primer binds {expected} {uniq}at {coord} (sense strand)\")\n        else:\n            sentences.append(f\"forward primer has no exact match in {expected}\")\n        if rhits:\n            coord = \", \".join(f\"{p}-{p + L_r - 1}\" for p in rhits)\n            uniq = \"uniquely \" if len(rhits) == 1 else \"\"\n            sentences.append(f\"reverse primer (reverse-complemented) binds {expected} {uniq}at {coord}\")\n        else:\n            sentences.append(f\"reverse primer (reverse-complemented) has no exact match in {expected}\")\n    else:\n        sentences.append(f\"expected transcript {expected} is not present among supplied sequences\")\n\n    # ---- amplicon / status\n    amp_len = \"\"\n    if pair.get(\"input_issue\"):\n        status = \"malformed_input\"\n        sentences.append(pair[\"input_issue\"])\n    elif exp_rec is None:\n        status = \"expected_transcript_missing\"\n    elif not matched:\n        status = \"no_binding\"\n        fwd_anywhere = any(audit[\"fwd_hits\"].values())\n        rev_anywhere = any(audit[\"rev_hits\"].values())\n        if not fwd_anywhere:\n            sentences.append(\"forward primer matches none of the supplied transcripts\")\n        if not rev_anywhere:\n            sentences.append(\"reverse-complemented reverse primer matches none of the supplied transcripts\")\n        sentences.append(\"no amplicon can be formed on any supplied isoform\")\n    elif not exp_amps:\n        status = \"off_target\"\n        first = matched[0]\n        amp_len = audit[\"amplicons\"][first][0][\"length\"]\n        sentences.append(f\"amplicon formed only on non-expected transcript(s): {'; '.join(matched)}\")\n    else:\n        if len(exp_amps) > 1 or len(audit[\"fwd_hits\"][expected]) > 1 or len(audit[\"rev_hits\"][expected]) > 1:\n            status = \"ambiguous\"\n            amp_len = exp_amps[0][\"length\"]\n            sentences.append(f\"{len(exp_amps)} candidate amplicons on {expected}; primer binding is not unique\")\n        else:\n            amp = exp_amps[0]\n            amp_len = amp[\"length\"]\n            sentences.append(f\"predicted amplicon {expected}:{amp['start']}-{amp['end']} length {amp['length']} bp\")\n            if expected_bp is not None and amp[\"length\"] != expected_bp:\n                status = \"length_mismatch\"\n                sentences.append(f\"amplicon length {amp['length']} bp differs from expected {expected_bp} bp (delta {amp['length'] - expected_bp:+d} bp)\")\n            else:\n                status tentative on cds below\n    # ---- cds compatibility\n    if exp_rec is not None and exp_amps:\n        cds_value, cds_expl = cds_compatible_verdict(exp_rec, exp_amps)\n    else:\n        cds_value, cds_expl = \"na\", \"no amplicon on the expected transcript\"\n```\n\nAnd if length matched (no status assigned yet):\n\n```python\n                if cds_value == \"yes\":\n                    status = \"pass\"\n                elif cds_value == \"inconsistent_metadata\":\n                    status = \"metadata_conflict\"\n                else:\n                    status = \"cds_incompatible\"\n```\n\nCareful with control flow — status must always be assigned. Let me restructure with an explicit variable.\n\nAlso add specificity sentence: other transcripts tested:\n\n```python\n    other = [r[\"id\"] for r in records if r[\"id\"] != expected]\n    if exp_rec is not None and other:\n        off = [t for t in other if t in audit[\"amplicons\"]]\n        if off:\n            sentences.append(f\"also amplifies: {'; '.join(off)} (not isoform-specific)\")\n        else:\n            sentences.append(f\"no amplicon on other supplied transcript(s): {'; '.join(other)}\")\n```\n\nMetadata sentence:\n\n```python\n    if exp_rec is not None and (exp_rec[\"cds_issues\"] or exp_rec[\"seq_issues\"]):\n        for issue in exp_rec[\"seq_issues\"] + exp_rec[\"cds_issues\"]:\n            sentences.append(f\"{expected} header metadata issue (reported, not repaired): {issue}\")\n```\n\nAnd the face-value note for cds explanation — put inside cds_compatible_verdict:\n\n```python\n    if rec[\"cds_issues\"]:\n        s, e = rec[\"cds\"]\n        extra = \"\"\n        if all(a[\"start\"] >= s and a[\"end\"] <= e for a in amps):\n            extra = \"; even taking the annotation at face value the amplicon would fall inside the CDS, but the annotation itself contradicts the sequence length\"\n        else:\n            extra = (f\"; even taking the annotation at face value, the amplicon \"\n        